# C# style

- PascalCase: types, methods, public members. camelCase: locals and private fields (`_db` only if stored; prefer primary constructors).
- Interfaces: `I` prefix (`IAuthService`). Constants: PascalCase (`MaxSearchRows`), not SCREAMING_SNAKE.
- File name equals the primary type: `CustomerService.cs` → `CustomerService`.
- Use `var` when the type is obvious. Prefer LINQ, pattern matching, null-conditional, interpolation, records for immutable DTOs.
- `async`/`await` for all I/O. Pass `CancellationToken`. Avoid `.Result` / `.Wait()`.
- Throw `InvalidOperationException` (Vietnamese message) for business failures; do not use exceptions as normal control flow.
- Keep feature services small and constructor-injected. Ports belong in `Abstractions`; do not create catch-all helpers or new up `HmaDbContext` inside methods.
- Eager-load with `Include` when the caller needs navigations. Always `Take(...)` on unbounded search.
- New tests: xUnit + NSubstitute (or Moq), next to behavior they lock (freight, sequences, amount-in-words, permissions).

```csharp
// BAD
public async void Save() => db.SaveChanges();

// GOOD
public async Task SaveAsync(SaveCustomerCommand command, CancellationToken ct = default)
{
    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(command.Code))
        throw new InvalidOperationException("Mã khách hàng là bắt buộc.");
    await db.SaveChangesAsync(ct);
}
```
